# EyeComfort Shader 1.0
profile.NEUTRO=Neutral
profile.SUAVE=Soft
profile.DESCANSO=Eye Comfort
profile.NOCHE=Night
profile.comment=Neutral: original colors. Soft: subtle warmth. Eye Comfort: balanced warmth and softer whites. Night: warmer and dimmer.
option.FILTER_STRENGTH=Filter Strength
option.FILTER_STRENGTH.comment=0 bypasses the color filter; 1 applies all adjustments. Compare with the image before filtering.
option.TEMPERATURE=Color Temperature
option.TEMPERATURE.comment=Lower values give a warmer image. 6500 is neutral. Kelvin values are approximate, not monitor calibration.
suffix.TEMPERATURE=\ K
option.CONTRAST=Contrast
option.CONTRAST.comment=1 is neutral. Lower values soften contrast; higher values increase it while preserving black and white endpoints.
option.BLACK_LEVEL=Blacks / Pedestal
option.BLACK_LEVEL.comment=Raises the black level before tinting. 0 preserves black; 0.025 adds a subtle lift. Does not recover missing detail.
option.WHITE_LEVEL=Whites / Maximum Level
option.WHITE_LEVEL.comment=Sets the upper limit before tinting. 1 is neutral; lower values reduce the tonal range above the black pedestal.
option.HIGHLIGHTS=Highlight Compression
option.HIGHLIGHTS.comment=0 is neutral. Higher values smoothly reduce bright tones, with a stronger effect on highlights.
option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.SATURATION.comment=1 preserves saturation; 0 removes original color before the warm tint. Try 0.85 for softer colors.
